      "content": "11. Independence of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The first session of the INC was held in December 1885 at Gokuldas Tejpal Sanskrit College, Bombay, attended by 72 delegates.",
        "Lord Curzon announced the Partition of Bengal in 1905, which led to the origin of the Swadeshi Movement.",
        "Mahatma Gandhi withdrew the Non-Cooperation Movement in February 1922 following the violent Chauri Chaura incident.",
        "The Mountbatten Plan of June 3, 1947, laid down the framework for the partition and independence of India and Pakistan."
      ],
      "id": "j6wlz4u"
